# What a build and a run of this repository leave behind.
#
# This file is tracked, so the rules reach a clone: without it a reader who
# builds the binaries or brings a deployment up finds the results sitting in
# `git status` with nothing to say they are disposable.

# Binaries. bin/ ships its README and nothing else. The Volantis binaries are a
# release archive to unpack here; `gtp5g-tunnel` and UERANSIM are other people's
# projects, cloned and built by whoever runs this. None of the three belongs in
# a git history — see bin/README.md.
bin/*
!bin/README.md

# Both runners' working directory, beside the scripts that write it: logs, pid
# files, the profiles uegen writes, and everything rendered from a template.
# deploy/run/external/ is the out-of-cluster half. Anchored rather than a bare
# `run/`, which would also swallow a directory of that name anywhere else in the
# tree — including one a future src/ might carry.
/deploy/run/

# The kustomize overlay k8s-deploy.sh generates to pin the image tag. It lives
# inside manifest/ because a kustomization can only reference a base at a fixed
# relative distance.
/deploy/k8s/manifest/.deploy/

# Editor and OS leavings. Not speculative: a stray .k8s-deploy.sh.swp from an
# open editor is what prompted the rule.
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store

# Maintainer notes for Claude Code — the decisions behind CLAUDE.md, the lab's
# verification runs, dates. CLAUDE.md ships as the rules; this is the history
# behind them and is not something a reader of the artifacts needs.
/.claude/
